CtrlCore/CtrlCore.h: CtrlCore/CtrlCore.h defines U++’s core GUI framework: controls and windows, input and event handling, layout frames, timers, clipboard and drag-and-drop, drawing interfaces, and platform integration.
CtrlCore/MKeys.h: CtrlCore/MKeys.h defines U++ keyboard shortcut constants for combinations of keys with Ctrl, Shift, and Alt, covering navigation, editing, function keys, letters, and digits.
CtrlCore/TopWindow.h: CtrlCore/TopWindow.h declares `Upp::TopWindow`, the base class for top-level GUI windows and dialogs. It provides window styles, state and layout controls, title-bar behavior, and helpers for arranging standard dialog buttons.
CtrlCore/Win32Gui.h: Declares U++’s Win32 GUI drawing backend: GDI-based screen, printer, image, and buffered drawing, plus enhanced metafile support and drawing helpers. It also defines Windows-specific control, clipboard, keycode, and platform include hooks.
CtrlCore/Gtk.h: CtrlCore/Gtk.h provides GTK-specific GUI integration for U++’s CtrlCore: platform drawing, window and control handling, events, clipboard, drag-and-drop, application setup, and GTK utility interfaces.
CtrlCore/Coco.h: CtrlCore/Coco.h provides the macOS Cocoa platform integration for U++’s CtrlCore GUI layer, defining platform-specific interfaces and types used to connect controls, windows, drawing, events, and clipboard behavior to Cocoa.
